# AI Tool Kart — Client environment.
#
# Copy to `client/.env.local` and adjust. `.env.local` is gitignored (`*.local`);
# this file is the only tracked client env file.
#
# ── EVERYTHING HERE IS PUBLIC ────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Vite compiles every VITE_-prefixed variable into the browser bundle, in plain
# text, for anyone to read. A secret placed here is a published secret.
#
# So there is no VITE_LLM_API_KEY, no VITE_ANTHROPIC_API_KEY and no
# VITE_OPENAI_API_KEY, and there never will be: the browser talks only to the
# AI Tool Kart backend, and the backend is the only process that ever holds a
# model credential (see server/.env.example, LLM_API_KEY).

# ─── The AI Tool Kart API ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Base URL of the server in server/, INCLUDING the /api path. Read once at
# module scope by src/services/http.ts, which every service module goes through.
#
# Optional in development: services/http.ts falls back to this exact value,
# which is the port server/.env.example fixes. Set it in every deployment.
VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:3001/api

# ─── WordPress (blog content) ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The headless CMS behind /blog. REQUIRED — services/wordpress.ts throws when it
# is missing rather than guessing someone else's host. The blog pages degrade to
# an error state; the rest of the site is unaffected.
VITE_WORDPRESS_API_URL=http://ai-tool-kart-cms.local/wp-json/wp/v2
